1
00:00:06,060 --> 00:00:11,770
We were three cities. One of gold, one of silver, one of iron.

2
00:00:11,820 --> 00:00:15,930
The story is named not after our kings, but after us: Tripura.

3
00:00:15,980 --> 00:00:18,650
And so is the name of the one who killed us: Tripurari.

4
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:23,850
Demons are killed, not cities. So why is Shiva called the enemy of cities?

5
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:27,850
Listen to the end. Then you will know where we are today.

6
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:37,090
The father of our kings was Tarakasura.

7
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:45,810
He had asked: let only a son of Shiva kill me. He thought Shiva, who burned Kama, would never be a father.

8
00:00:45,860 --> 00:00:48,770
Skanda was born. Tarakasura was killed.

9
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:54,450
Three sons were left. Tarakaksha the eldest, Vidyunmali the middle, Kamalaksha the youngest.

10
00:00:54,500 --> 00:01:00,850
They learnt nothing from their father's mistake. Only this: ask for a bigger boon.

11
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:07,650
Prahlada heard Narada while still in his mother's womb, and learnt. Our kings heard, and did not.

12
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:10,130
In a cave of Meru, the penance began.

13
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:16,450
A hundred years on one foot. A thousand years living on air. A thousand years upside down.

14
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:18,450
And Brahma appeared.

15
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:24,250
They said: let no one kill us. Let neither old age nor death come.

16
00:01:24,380 --> 00:01:31,930
Brahma said: the soul does not die, but a body that is born must go. Choose some cause of your death.

17
00:01:31,980 --> 00:01:38,530
And they laughed at Brahma: lotus-born! You too were born; you too will go.

18
00:01:38,580 --> 00:01:46,890
Still, Brahma kept a big heart. Bhishma was given death at will, for dharma. They too were given the freedom: choose your own death.

19
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:49,770
Then, after a moment's thought, they asked for three cities.

20
00:01:49,820 --> 00:01:58,330
Gold for Tarakaksha, in heaven. Silver for Kamalaksha, in the sky. Iron for Vidyunmali, on earth.

21
00:01:58,380 --> 00:02:00,490
And they set the condition themselves.

22
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:10,770
After a thousand years, at midday in Abhijit, with the moon in Pushya, while the Pushkara and Avarta clouds rain, the three cities will come together for one moment.

23
00:02:10,820 --> 00:02:19,050
In that moment, one in whom all the gods dwell, seated on an impossible chariot, must pierce us with one impossible arrow. Only then will we die.

24
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:22,890
Brahma remembered Shiva, and said: so be it.

25
00:02:22,940 --> 00:02:28,090
And leaving, he said: no one has ever asked for such a boon. Handle it with care.

26
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:31,170
Maya the danava built us.

27
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:39,010
Within us were wish-trees, elephants, horses, flying cars. A Shiva-linga in every house, a sacred fire in every house.

28
00:02:39,060 --> 00:02:41,490
A sinner could not even see us.

29
00:02:41,540 --> 00:02:45,530
Then we began to circle. Without stopping. So that everyone would see.

30
00:02:45,820 --> 00:02:48,410
The gods lost. Amaravati was taken.

31
00:02:48,460 --> 00:02:57,450
Indra was told: rain when we say. The Sun: burn softly when we go out. The Moon: rise by day.

32
00:02:57,500 --> 00:02:59,610
The seasons lost their meaning.

33
00:02:59,660 --> 00:03:04,450
Not one leaf could fall even in winter; we wanted spring everywhere.

34
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:12,330
That is the drunkenness of bodily strength. Every day it needs someone weak, to beat, to feel strong.

35
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:18,570
The gods went to Brahma. Brahma said: they have three strengths.

36
00:03:18,620 --> 00:03:24,490
The boon I gave. The strength of their own bodies. And the third: devotion to Shiva.

37
00:03:24,540 --> 00:03:29,050
And also: I myself raised this daitya; how can I kill him?

38
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:32,810
The gods reached Kailasa. Shiva listened, and said:

39
00:03:32,860 --> 00:03:40,170
Those daityas are my devotees. From dawn to night they take my name. I will not kill them. Go to Vishnu.

40
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:45,050
Vishnu performed a sacrifice. Thousands of bhuta-ganas rose from the fire, armed.

41
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:50,730
They entered us, and like moths in a flame, they burned in our radiance.

42
00:03:50,780 --> 00:03:56,837
Then Vishnu understood: as long as they stand on Vedic dharma and the Shiva-linga, no one can kill them.

43
00:03:56,887 --> 00:03:59,130
So their dharma itself must fall.

44
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:03,850
From his own body, Vishnu created a man.

45
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:17,050
A shaven head, dirty clothes, a wooden vessel, a broom to sweep the ground at every step, a cloth over his mouth, and one word on his lips: dharma, dharma.

46
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:20,050
Vishnu said: your name will be Arihan.

47
00:04:20,100 --> 00:04:28,250
Make a scripture of sixteen thousand verses, against shruti and smriti, sweet to hear, like poison smeared with honey.

48
00:04:28,300 --> 00:04:34,010
He came to us. No one stopped to listen. Before our Shiva-worship, his maya failed.

49
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:36,130
Then Vishnu sent Narada.

50
00:04:36,180 --> 00:04:45,410
Narada first took initiation from that shaven one himself. Then he told Tarakaksha: a great soul has come to your kingdom. I have never seen such a dharma.

51
00:04:45,460 --> 00:04:47,930
Narada was saying it, so we believed.

52
00:04:47,980 --> 00:04:53,250
Tarakaksha was initiated. Then his brothers. Then every soul in the three cities.

53
00:04:54,420 --> 00:05:00,930
He taught: there is no creator, no karma. Heaven is here, and hell is here.

54
00:05:00,980 --> 00:05:07,410
Brahma, Vishnu, Mahesha are only names. You burn sesame and ghee and hope for heaven?

55
00:05:07,460 --> 00:05:12,610
This body is food for dogs and crows. While it is healthy, enjoy it.

56
00:05:12,660 --> 00:05:18,850
Hungry and strong? Snatch and eat. Sin after death? Did anyone come back to tell?

57
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:24,450
Caste is a lie. And the rules of marriage? Kashyapa married thirteen sisters.

58
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:32,410
And our king proclaimed: no kinship, no bounds, no wife, no child. Whoever wants whatever, take it.

59
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:36,930
We abandoned the Shiva-lingas. We abandoned shraddha, sacrifice, vows.

60
00:05:36,980 --> 00:05:41,890
Wives abandoned their husbands. Men worked spells of control on other men's wives.

61
00:05:41,940 --> 00:05:45,170
Day and night, only wealth and lust.

62
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:50,770
Alakshmi came in. Lakshmi left. And the strength of our kings dried up.

63
00:05:50,820 --> 00:05:55,730
The fault was not the speaker's. The fault was the listeners'. Ours.

64
00:05:57,500 --> 00:06:01,850
Standing in water, Vishnu chanted the Rudra mantra fifteen million times.

65
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:08,863
Shiva came, and still he hesitated: they were my devotees. Vishnu made them fall; let Vishnu kill them.

66
00:06:08,913 --> 00:06:12,410
Brahma said: a king's dharma is to protect dharma.

67
00:06:12,540 --> 00:06:18,010
Shiva said: I am the emperor, but I have no chariot, no bow, no arrow.

68
00:06:18,060 --> 00:06:20,090
The gods said: we will become them.

69
00:06:20,140 --> 00:06:27,370
Then Shiva went inside, gazing at Skanda's face. At the door, the gana Kumbhodara beat the gods with a staff.

70
00:06:27,420 --> 00:06:38,650
The gods chanted ten million times: Om namah Shivaya, shubham shubham kuru kuru, Shivaya namah Om. And Shiva appeared again, and Vishwakarma built the chariot.

71
00:06:38,700 --> 00:06:48,930
The right wheel the Sun, the twelve Adityas its spokes. The left wheel the Moon, its sixteen phases. The six seasons the rims. The year its speed.

72
00:06:48,980 --> 00:06:53,530
Brahma the charioteer. Om the whip. The four Vedas the horses.

73
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:58,530
Sumeru the bow. Shesha the bowstring. Saraswati the bell of the bow.

74
00:06:58,580 --> 00:07:02,730
And the arrow, Vishnu himself. Its tip, Agni.

75
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:11,770
Shiva looked at the chariot, and laughed. A chariot of earth; when the Sun goes forward, the Moon goes back. But he said nothing.

76
00:07:11,820 --> 00:07:19,370
God accepts anything made with devotion, like the children's chariot of beans on Ratha Saptami.

77
00:07:19,580 --> 00:07:24,570
Shiva mounted the chariot. And the horses fell on their heads. The earth shook.

78
00:07:24,620 --> 00:07:29,130
The Vedas can point towards Brahman. They cannot carry him.

79
00:07:29,260 --> 00:07:34,290
Shesha took the form of a bull, lifted the chariot for one moment, and fell to his knees.

80
00:07:34,340 --> 00:07:44,130
Tradition says Vishnu himself then became the bull, and pulled. Shankaracharya wrote: banatvam, vrishabhatvam. He became the arrow, and the bull.

81
00:07:44,180 --> 00:07:55,770
Before setting out, Shiva said: accept that you are all my pashus. The gods were afraid. Shiva laughed: whoever keeps the Pashupata vow will be freed. From that day he was called Pashupati.

82
00:07:55,820 --> 00:07:57,610
The chariot moved towards the sky.

83
00:07:57,660 --> 00:08:02,490
And we? We were laughing in the sky. What can he kill in a single moment?

84
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:09,370
Shiva fitted the arrow, and stood. A hundred thousand years. Unmoving.

85
00:08:09,420 --> 00:08:14,890
Because Ganesha sat on his thumb, and the cities never came into his aim.

86
00:08:14,940 --> 00:08:18,010
A voice from the sky: first, worship the lord of obstacles.

87
00:08:18,140 --> 00:08:21,370
Shiva called Bhadrakali, and worshipped Ganesha.

88
00:08:21,420 --> 00:08:24,490
And in that very moment, the three of us became one.

89
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:27,890
The gods said: you could burn them with a single glance.

90
00:08:27,940 --> 00:08:32,010
Shiva's face turned red. The third eyelid stirred. Then he stopped.

91
00:08:32,140 --> 00:08:38,570
Vishnu, Soma, Kalagni and Vayu, inside the arrow, said: Lord, for our sake, release the arrow.

92
00:08:38,620 --> 00:08:40,170
And Shiva laughed.

93
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:49,003
Abhijit muhurta. Shiva drew the bow, twanged the string, called out his own name.

94
00:08:49,733 --> 00:08:52,483
The arrow flew, like ten million suns.

95
00:08:53,413 --> 00:09:02,763
The golden city melted first. The walls we were so proud of boiled and poured over us: gold clinging to skin, sinking into flesh.

96
00:09:02,813 --> 00:09:07,683
Silver boiled and flooded the courtyards. Those standing there, their feet set in it.

97
00:09:07,733 --> 00:09:12,843
The iron city turned red, then white. The screams inside were seared into the metal.

98
00:09:12,893 --> 00:09:15,003
The hair burned first, then the eyes.

99
00:09:15,053 --> 00:09:20,803
Those who ran turned to ash running: one step of flesh, the next of smoke.

100
00:09:20,853 --> 00:09:24,643
The old, who could not even rise, became charcoal in their beds.

101
00:09:24,693 --> 00:09:30,723
Mothers crushed their children to their breasts, and the fire made both a single fistful of ash.

102
00:09:30,773 --> 00:09:33,763
Women asleep in their husbands' arms never even woke.

103
00:09:33,813 --> 00:09:39,763
Elephants, horses, flying cars, everything. The fire did not stop. The command was: let nothing remain.

104
00:09:39,893 --> 00:09:48,243
And burning, Tarakaksha remembered Shiva: O Bhava, birth after birth, let our minds dwell in devotion to you.

105
00:09:51,413 --> 00:09:55,283
The three of us fell to earth together, as ash.

106
00:09:55,413 --> 00:09:59,123
The drums of the gods sounded, and flowers rained on Shiva.

107
00:09:59,173 --> 00:10:05,443
Only Maya survived, who even in disaster had taken refuge in Shiva. Shiva sent him to Vitala.

108
00:10:05,493 --> 00:10:10,163
Those who were still worshipping Shiva as they burned became lords of his ganas.

109
00:10:10,213 --> 00:10:17,923
And the shaven ones? Vishnu said: hide in the desert until Kali. In Kali, whoever takes up this teaching will be ruined.

110
00:10:17,973 --> 00:10:23,363
Patanjali called Shiva akhanda-daya: the one who burned Tripura out of boundless compassion.

111
00:10:23,413 --> 00:10:27,843
Burning out of compassion? Yes. Because we were never in the sky.

112
00:10:28,960 --> 00:10:36,163
We are within you. The gross body, the subtle body, the causal body. Waking, dream, deep sleep.

113
00:10:36,213 --> 00:10:41,123
In these three you circle your whole life, without stopping, as we circled.

114
00:10:41,173 --> 00:10:50,163
There is a fourth: turiya, which watches all three. Ramana Maharshi was asked, do you sleep? He said: I am the witness of sleep.

115
00:10:50,213 --> 00:10:56,723
Shankaracharya says: make the mind a balance. The whole world in one pan, the Lord in the other.

116
00:10:56,773 --> 00:11:04,203
An empty balance sways in a breeze. But if the Lord sits in one pan, put anything in the other and it will not lift.

117
00:11:04,253 --> 00:11:11,363
Let joy come, let sorrow come; if the pan does not move, the Lord lifts the arrow. And that day, your Tripura burns.

118
00:11:11,413 --> 00:11:20,043
We asked for a boon to escape death. Sanatana asks: like a ripe cucumber from its stalk, let me be freed.

119
00:11:20,093 --> 00:11:26,043
Every night before sleep, count how many times you wavered today. Then take his name eleven times.

120
00:11:27,946 --> 00:11:31,043
We were Tripura. He is Tripurari.
